    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Developer Overview – FOI Payment Expiry SLA Job\n\n**Purpose:**\nExpires online fee payments that the applicant didn't complete by the payment expiry date. It replaces the old long-running Wait (20-day timeout).\n\n**Trigger/Entry:**\nSchedule trigger, every day 1 PM(runs only while the workflow is active).\n\n**Processing:**\nReads the `foi-payment-sla` rows where sla_type = payment-expiry and sla_status = ACTIVE, then applies the Camunda timer rule: keep a row only when floor(|now - payment_expiry_date| / 1 day) == 0, i.e. the run is within 24 hours of that date, before or after (confirmed by the FOI team). Older payments get no expiry notice and stay ACTIVE, so a late payment or cancellation is still processed. A missed window is not caught up, and a row without a payment_expiry_date never expires. Each payment is notified once, because an expired row is no longer ACTIVE. Builds one `foi-payment-expired` event per row (feeAction = expire, paymentStatus = EXPIRED), each from its own row's metadata.\n\n**Integration/Outcome:**\nCalls FOI Fee Processing once per expired payment. That workflow first checks the latest payment version: an unpaid, not cancelled payment gets the expiry notification and its SLA row is marked EXPIRED; an already paid or cancelled payment has its row closed as PAID / CANCELLED with no notification.",
        "height": 568,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "08897511-709a-4c86-848e-00c6cf863f03",
      "name": "Developer Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
